# Layout System Architecture Guide

## Core Architecture

```
/_authenticated (Route)
├── GlobalSidebar (64px fixed)
└── SidebarLayout (Unified)
    ├── SidebarProvider (Shadcn context)
    ├── AppSidebar (Dynamic content)
    └── SidebarInset
        ├── Header (Context-aware)
        └── Main Content (Outlet)
            └── ContentContainer (REQUIRED for all pages)
```

## Required Page Pattern
```typescript
import { ContentContainer } from '@/components/layout/content-container'

function MyPage() {
  return (
    <ContentContainer>
      <div className="space-y-6">
        <div>
          <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Page Title</h1>
          <p className="text-muted-foreground">Page description</p>
        </div>
        {/* Page content */}
      </div>
    </ContentContainer>
  )
}
```

## Section Configuration
- **layoutStore.ts**: Add section to `sectionConfig` + route detection in `updateSectionFromRoute`
- **sidebar-data.ts**: Add section to `globalSidebarData` array

## Anti-Patterns (NEVER)
```typescript
// ❌ Manual layout components
<div className="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4"> // Use ContentContainer instead

// ❌ Multiple state systems
const [sidebarOpen, setSidebarOpen] = useState(false) // Use SidebarProvider

// ❌ Manual width calculations
const contentWidth = `calc(100vw - ${sidebarWidth}px)` // Use LayoutStore

// ❌ Content based on pending section
const navGroups = getSidebarDataForSection(pendingSection || activeSection) // Use activeSection only
```

## Adding New Pages

### Existing Section
1. Create route file with ContentContainer
2. Add to sidebar-data.ts navigation

### New Section
1. Add to `sectionConfig` in layoutStore.ts
2. Add route detection logic in `updateSectionFromRoute`
3. Add to `globalSidebarData` in sidebar-data.ts
4. Create routes with ContentContainer

### No-Sidebar Pages
1. Set `showSidebar: false` in section config
2. Set `showMainSidebar: false` in global sidebar data
3. Still use ContentContainer

## Route Template
```typescript
import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'
import { ContentContainer } from '@/components/layout/content-container'

export const Route = createFileRoute('/_authenticated/my-page')({
  component: MyPage,
})

function MyPage() {
  return (
    <ContentContainer>
      <div className="space-y-6">
        <div>
          <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Title</h1>
          <p className="text-muted-foreground">Description</p>
        </div>
        {/* Content */}
      </div>
    </ContentContainer>
  )
}
```

## Essential Rules
- **ALWAYS** use ContentContainer for page layouts
- **NEVER** create manual width/padding constraints
- Use `activeSection` not `pendingSection` for content
- Memoize derived values with `useMemo`
- Icons from `lucide-react`
